                                                "sense_id": "1ad83db3-9409-3d1b-a417-8c8bc208aa3e",
                                                "text": "In 1905, Harden and Young found that the zymase of Buchner consisted of a thermolabile ferment fraction, which was later designated as \"apo-zymase\" by Neuberg and v. Euler, and of a thermostable ultrafiltrable factor, \"co-zymase,\" the presence of which is necessary for the fermentation of sugar."
                                            }
